throws intl Intl.getCanonicalLocales Intl.supportedValuesOf String.prototype.localeCompare Number.prototype.toLocaleString BigInt.prototype.toLocaleString Date.prototype.toLocaleString Date.prototype.toLocaleDateString Date.prototype.toLocaleTimeString
about intl All of `Intl`, `localeCompare()`, and `toLocaleString()`, `toLocaleDateString()` and `toLocaleTimeString()`, with the locale data behind them. On macOS Bun uses the system's ICU, so there only the bindings go. For now a call of `localeCompare()` or of one of the three `toLocale` functions of a number or a date in code that was compiled ahead of time (`compile.aot`) does not throw: it ends the process with exit code 70.
